{"name":"Diva","hex":"#c9a0ff","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"diva","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any female celebrity, usually a well known singer or actress. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A person with an inflated sense of self, who has high expectations of others, and who is extremely demanding and fussy when it comes to personal privileges."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diva"}],"entries":[{"title":"Diva","blocks":[{"text":"Diva, the Latin word for a goddess, has often been used as an honorific to refer to a celebrated woman of outstanding talent in the world of opera, theatre, cinema, fashion and popular music. If referring to an actress, the meaning of diva is closely related to that of prima donna. Diva can also refer to a person, especially one in show business, with a reputation for being temperamental or demanding. The application of the term has broadened beyond the performing arts to also include celebrated political and business figures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Mariah_Carey_-_Beautiful_%28Live_%40_GMA%2C_May_24%2C_2013%29.JPG/330px-Mariah_Carey_-_Beautiful_%28Live_%40_GMA%2C_May_24%2C_2013%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diva","wikidata":"Q867132"},{"title":"Diva (Annie Lennox album)","blocks":[{"text":"Diva is the debut solo studio album by Scottish singer Annie Lennox, released on 6 April 1992 by RCA Records. The album entered the UK Albums Chart at number one and has since sold over 1.2 million copies in the UK alone, being certified quadruple platinum. Diva was the 7th best selling album of 1992 in the United Kingdom. In the United States, it reached number 23 on the Billboard 200 and has been certified double platinum."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/89/Annie_Lennox_-_Diva_Album_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diva_(Annie_Lennox_album)","wikidata":"Q625882"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Eurythmics_06101986_02_270.jpg/250px-Eurythmics_06101986_02_270.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5e/Eurythmics_06101986_02_270.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Eurythmics_06101986_02_270.jpg/250px-Eurythmics_06101986_02_270.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lennox in 1986. Following the informal dissolution of Eurythmics in 1990, Lennox began working on Diva in 1991","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEurythmics_06101986_02_270.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/fb/Annie_Lennox_-_The_Gift_shot.png/330px-Annie_Lennox_-_The_Gift_shot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/fb/Annie_Lennox_-_The_Gift_shot.png/330px-Annie_Lennox_-_The_Gift_shot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lennox in character as \"the Diva\" in the music video for \"The Gift\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnnie_Lennox_-_The_Gift_shot.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/DSC_4708_%287777760762%29.jpg/500px-DSC_4708_%287777760762%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/DSC_4708_%287777760762%29.jpg/1280px-DSC_4708_%287777760762%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/DSC_4708_%287777760762%29.jpg/500px-DSC_470